--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@ To merge the simulation models of CAN and FlexRay significant changes were neces
 ### CAN
 It is possible to create networks with traffic consisting of Data-, Remote- and Error-Frames. To get some variation in the transmit and receive times of cyclic messages it is possible to simulate a clock drift.
 
+CAN FD data frames are supported with 11- or 29-bit identifiers, legal DLC values, up to 64-byte payloads, and optional bit-rate switching. Set `fdCapable`, `arbitrationBitrate`, and `dataBitrate` on `CanBus`, then set `fd`, `bitRateSwitch`, and `extendedId` on a source application. The existing `bitStuffingPercentage` remains a percentage-based timing approximation: this is not a bit-exact CAN physical-layer model. CAN FD remote frames and CAN FD error injection are rejected because their timing is not modeled.
+
 The arbitration ensures that the frame with the highest priority is transmitted as soon as several nodes try to transmit their messages.
 
 
