@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# CAN FD example
+
+`BRSOff` and `BRSOn` send a 64-byte standard-ID CAN FD frame at 500 kbit/s
+arbitration rate. `BRSOn` switches its data phase to 2 Mbit/s and therefore
+finishes sooner. `InvalidPayload` and `InvalidFdRemote` intentionally fail
+during initialization, exercising validation of unsupported CAN FD payload
+lengths and remote frames.
+
+Timing uses FiCo4OMNeT's configurable percentage-based stuffing approximation;
+it does not simulate individual stuffed bits or a physical layer.
